v3.2.12
Radon Player 3.2.12: A steadier DJ and Bluetooth fixes
## 3.2.12: A steadier DJ and Bluetooth fixes (Windows and Android)
- **Newest Bluetooth device wins (Settings › Playback, under Ignore Bluetooth devices):** with two Bluetooth devices connected (an earbud you set down in the truck, then the truck), the one that connected last has the music, the DJ and its own EQ, instead of the one that was there first. Android Auto counts as a device. They work together: a device you ignore never gets the music, even when it's the newest. Apps can't disconnect a device, so the other one stays connected for calls, but nothing plays on it. On the PC too.
- **Ignore Bluetooth devices works with Android Auto:** with the car ignored, Android Auto (wired or wireless) still took the music, since its sound isn't a Bluetooth output. Now the car's screen keeps the map, calls and the rest, while the music and the DJ's voice play on your headphones (Bluetooth ones you haven't ignored, else wired). It knows the car by its Bluetooth name (also when it's only connected for calls), or pick Android Auto itself in the list. With no headphones connected, the music stays on the car.
- **No more music stopping by itself in the background:** after any pause (one of the DJ's, a call, a moment's pause of yours), Android took the app out of the foreground, and with the screen off it wouldn't let it back in when the music went on ("startForegroundService() not allowed"), so the music stopped. The app now stays a foreground player for 10 minutes after a pause, so Play from your headphones, the car or the lock screen, and the DJ's next set, always carry on. Paused longer than that, it lets go as before.
- **The DJ keeps going on its own:** between sets the music was paused while the DJ's line was made and said, and with the screen off Android could take the app out of the background in that pause, so the DJ stopped by itself. Nothing pauses now: the set's first song waits at its start under the line with its volume all the way down, so you hear only her (Now playing's time moves while she talks), then plays from the top. A crossfade's ending song is cut off when she starts, and with Bit-perfect (which can't turn a song down) the song waits paused as before. Only you stop it.
- **The DJ talks straight away:** the next set's line is made in the background while the current set plays, so when a set begins she starts talking at once instead of after a long wait for the natural voice (or ElevenLabs). Switch it up is instant too: a set is always made ahead for it, line and all.
- **The DJ never gets stuck between sets:** skipping with your headphones' buttons into a new set could leave it paused with the DJ silent, and the headphones' Play did nothing (only the app's Play got it going). Play from the headphones, the car or the lock screen now does exactly what the app's Play does: a line that never came out is said again, a set it hadn't introduced gets its line, and one it was still picking goes on when it's ready (trying again if the lookup failed, rather than stopping). If the voice ever doesn't finish, the music starts anyway, and Pause on your headphones while the DJ talks stops her too.
- **The DJ's play counts are your real ones:** it counted an artist's and a song's plays only from the plays with a time the phone had read, so it could say Juice WRLD had 75 plays when you have far more. Everything the DJ goes by (its counts, sets and facts) now comes from Last.fm and your Spotify, Apple Music, Deezer, YouTube Music and Tidal imports, an artist's plays under one name. The plays counted in the app are only used when there's nothing from Last.fm or an import at all (they still keep a song you just played from coming straight back).
- **Skips never keep songs out of the DJ:** the DJ left out songs you'd skipped three times or more (more often than you heard them out). Skips don't change what it plays now (you may just not be in the mood for a song); they're only counted, for Skips and for the DJ to tell you about: your most skipped song, songs you've never skipped, how many you skipped this week and in all.

### Good to know
- **Android:** install RadonPlayer.apk over 3.2.11 (same signature, your library and settings stay), or tap Update in Settings. Setting the app's battery to Unrestricted (Settings › Apps › Radon Player › Battery) helps it keep playing with the screen off.
- **Windows:** Radon-Player-3.2.12.msi installs over 3.2.11, or use Update in Settings.
